abstract: >
  Policy Lab is a descriptive public interface for a case-based research workbench
  that evaluates how explicit evidence and policy rules block, bound, and settle
  financial claims. The software separates admission gates, comparable quantity
  ceilings, and settlement constraints; attributes blocking and binding rules;
  preserves deterministic decision identity under declared case, evidence,
  context, policy, and calculator inputs; and emits decision receipts for
  inspection and reproduction. A separate aggregate market-capacity study exposes
  historical policy trade-offs without redistributing licensed row-level data.
  SolarPunk Public Lab and the Energy Standard remain the original energy-linked
  digital-finance reference domain and Sepolia application. The software does not
  claim real operator validation, legal collateral or redemption rights, reserve
  custody, empirical geospatial policy superiority, production oracle finality,
  production governance, or mainnet readiness.
